📘 Amazon Connect Flow Deployment – Developer Guide
This guide outlines the standardized process for developing and deploying Amazon Connect Flows and Flow Modules across multiple environments using CDK automation.
🔁 Overview
Our automation ensures that flows and modules can be exported from the Connect GUI and deployed without manual changes by dynamically transforming references to:
Lambda ARNs
Contact Flow ARNs
Flow Module IDs
URLs
📂 Project Structure
config/
  ├── dev1/
  │   └── connectInstance.json
  ├── qa1/
  │   └── connectInstance.json
  └── flows/
      ├── CONTACT_FLOW/
      │   └── welcomeFlow.json
      ├── AGENT_HOLD/
      │   └── holdFlow.json
      └── flowConfig.json
controller.json
scripts/
  ├── transformFlow.ts
  └── transformFlowModule.ts
🔄 How the Transformation Works
When running build.sh, the following occurs:
✅ Lambda ARNs are transformed using the stage/account info and mode from controller.json:

arn:aws:lambda:<region>:<accountId>:function:<resourceFullName>-G|B-<suffix>
✅ Contact Flow ARNs and Flow Module IDs are transformed to SSM references using display names from ActionMetaData.
✅ URLs like:

"https://api.cloud.net/dev1-lob"
are transformed to:
"https://${domainUrl}/${stage}-lob"
📄 SSM Parameter Strategy
We store reusable flow ARNs and module IDs in SSM Parameter Store, such as:
/dev1/flows/welcomeFlow/arn
/dev1/modules/holdModule/id
Then in your flow JSON, these are transformed as:
"ContactFlowId": "${ssm:/dev1/flows/welcomeFlow/arn}"
"FlowModuleId": "${ssm:/dev1/modules/holdModule/id}"
🧠 getSSMValue() in CDK Stack
In the AmazonConnectFlowStack, we resolve SSM paths like this:
const flowArn = getSSMValue(this, '/dev1/flows/welcomeFlow/arn');
const moduleId = getSSMValue(this, '/dev1/modules/holdModule/id');
This ensures dynamic resolution based on the environment being deployed.
⚠️ Flow Dependency Rules
Flows and modules that are referenced inside another flow must be created first.
Example:
If mainFlow.json references welcomeFlow, then welcomeFlow must be deployed first.
CDK manages this if flowConfig.json lists them in correct order.

🆔 Required: Identifiers in ActionMetaData
Any flow that references another flow or module must have the correct ActionMetaData.
Sample:
"ActionMetaData": {
  "111002": {
    "parameters": {
      "ContactFlowId": {
        "displayName": "welcomeFlow"
      }
    }
  }
},
"Actions": [
  {
    "Identifier": "111002",
    "Type": "TransferToFlow",
    "Parameters": {
      "ContactFlowId": "arn:aws:connect:..."
    }
  }
]
🟢 This tells the transformer to replace the ContactFlowId with a corresponding SSM reference.
📝 Developer Workflow
1. Export your flow/module from Amazon Connect.
2. Copy it into the appropriate folder:
config/flows/CONTACT_FLOW/
config/flows/AGENT_HOLD/
3. Update flowConfig.json:
"dev1": {
  "connect-instance": [
    "CONTACT_FLOW/welcomeFlow.json",
    "AGENT_HOLD/holdFlow.json"
  ]
}
4. ✅ Make sure:
The flow has Identifiers and ActionMetaData
Any reused flow/module has its SSM parameter created beforehand
5. ✅ Confirm controller.json mode is set:
{
  "lambda": "G" // or "B"
}
6. 🛠 Run build.sh
This will:
Transform Lambda ARNs
Insert ${ssm:/...} for ContactFlows and Modules
Rewrite any URLs with the environment name
7. 🚀 Trigger CDK Deployment:
cdk deploy --context stage=dev1
🧪 Example of Transformed JSON
{
  "Type": "TransferToFlow",
  "Identifier": "111002",
  "Parameters": {
    "ContactFlowId": "${ssm:/dev1/flows/welcomeFlow/arn}"
  }
}
🆘 Troubleshooting
No transformation? Ensure displayName is correctly defined.
Flow skipped? Check flowConfig.json and folder path.
Incorrect order? Make sure dependent flows/modules are created first.
